  "native": {
    "summary": "Where lymph returns to the blood. The cisterna chyli collects the intestinal and lumbar trunks in front of L1-L2; the thoracic duct climbs through the aortic hiatus and the posterior mediastinum, crosses to the left and empties into the left venous angle. The short right lymphatic duct takes the right jugular, subclavian and bronchomediastinal trunks to the right venous angle. Green = thoracic duct territory, teal = right lymphatic duct territory.",
